cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
type: software
title: "nrtqclib"
abstract: >-
  A Python library that runs near-real-time quality control (NRT QC) on CTD
  (Conductivity, Temperature, Depth) ocean profiles: it applies the automated
  real-time QC tests to temperature and salinity, writes one flag column per
  test and a final NRT flag per variable, and compares the new flags with the
  ones already in the data.
authors:
  - family-names: "Saito"
    given-names: "Takaya"
repository-code: "https://github.com/AIQC-Hub/nrtqclib"
url: "https://nrtqclib.readthedocs.io/"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - oceanography
  - CTD
  - quality control
  - near real time
  - Python
version: "0.1.6"
date-released: "2026-11-06"
